---
import AskQuack from '../islands/AskQuack';
---

<section id="model" class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-28 md:py-40">
  <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Quack-1 · our flagship model</p>
  <h2 class="h-section mt-4 max-w-3xl" data-reveal>
    Powered by AI<sup class="text-accent">*</sup>
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-cream-dim" data-reveal>
    Quack isn’t just a duck. It’s the result of unprecedented AI* breakthroughs: a fully open-weight
    (28 grams), on-device reasoning system with a context window of exactly one desk.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-xs text-cream-dim" data-reveal>* Aquatic Intelligence</p>

  <div class="mt-14 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2" data-reveal>
    <AskQuack client:visible />
    <div class="card flex flex-col justify-between p-6">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-4">model card</p>
        <dl class="space-y-3 font-mono text-sm">
          {
            [
              ['Parameters', '1 (yellow)'],
              ['Weights', '28 g, fully open'],
              ['Context window', '1 desk'],
              ['Output vocabulary', '1 token'],
              ['Determinism', 'absolute'],
              ['Power draw', '0 W'],
              ['Inference latency', '0 ms (pre-computed)'],
            ].map(([k, v]) => (
              <div class="flex justify-between gap-6 border-b border-cream/10 pb-3">
                <dt class="text-cream-dim">{k}</dt>
                <dd class="text-right">{v}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-xs text-cream-dim">
        AI fills in the gaps. We said “rubber duck debugging”. It heard “senior staff engineer”.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
